WEBVTT

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:07.590
In this video I want to show how you, as a farmer, can deal with keeping the calf with the cow for longer.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:13.230
Without constantly getting an alert about the calf walking around the pen, which is correct after all.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:19.150
We are at the cameras, and now we go to the detectors.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:23.750
There is one detector running: the Calving Catcher, which also looks for the calf.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:28.170
What we do now is go to the settings.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:33.450
Under the settings there is Advanced. We click it and this menu opens.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:43.170
This shows all the settings of the Calving Catcher, including those for the calf.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.990
There are two ways to tackle this problem.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:53.170
First, we can lengthen the time between alerts of a calf detection.

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:57.090
By default that is every 15 minutes.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:03.790
But we can lengthen it, for example to 3600 seconds.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:07.950
That would mean there has to be at least an hour between two alerts.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.350
And of course we can make it even longer.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:17.450
Any number of seconds is fine.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:25.330
In this case, 86,400 seconds is a cooldown period of one day.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:27.330
So within...

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.930
24 hours no new alert is sent.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:37.790
So after 24 hours, an alert for a calf detection may be sent again.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:40.130
And you can make this as long as you like.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:42.130
Make it three days, make it five days.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:44.130
The value is in seconds.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:50.130
Once you have changed it, in this case to one day, click Save here at the bottom left.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:55.070
It has been saved.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:02:00.890
A second way to tackle this is if you do not want any calf alerts at all.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.890
Or only want an alert of the calf in rare cases.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:10.890
What we change then is the value 0.85 under the heading confidence.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.890
The default value is replaced by 0.99.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:21.890
That is an unrealistically high threshold, so you will hardly get any calf detections any more.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:25.200
Then we click Save again.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:31.200
So with this configuration you will effectively get no calf alerts.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.200
Because the confidence for the calf...

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.200
Because the required confidence is far too high.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.200
Unrealistically high, even.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:46.200
But if a detection does still happen, there are at least 24 hours between alerts.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.200
Then we go to Monitoring.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.200
And you can see that all four cameras have started monitoring again.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.200
With the new settings.
